        <section class="section works-section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>What works today</h2>
                <p>The schematic document core runs from the CLI, SDK and native model. The interactive canvas and KiCad/Gerber exchange do not.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="works">
                <article class="works__col">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok"><span class="status-dot status-dot--on"></span>Available</span>
                    <h3>Document core</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Create, save and reopen one <code>.oeda</code> document</li>
                        <li>Add, move, update and delete components; connect nets, add and delete wires</li>
                        <li>Undo and redo with a bounded 32-step history per open document and a CLI sidecar that survives invocations</li>
                        <li>Add, rename and delete empty sheets; the last sheet is protected</li>
                        <li>ERC, net and footprint checks with located findings</li>
                        <li>Netlist, SVG, BOM and PDF projections written atomically</li>
                        <li>CLI editing of an existing document in place</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="works__col">
                    <span class="chip chip--ok"><span class="status-dot status-dot--on"></span>Available</span>
                    <h3>Contracts</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Handle-based design API</li>
                        <li>Revisioned design, sheets and objects</li>
                        <li>Stable namespaced error codes</li>
                        <li>Per-format import, edit and export matrix</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
                <article class="works__col">
                    <span class="chip chip--idle">Not implemented</span>
                    <h3>Not yet</h3>
                    <ul>
                        <li>Interactive canvas and sheet renderer</li>
                        <li>DRC, clearance and power checks</li>
                        <li>KiCad, Gerber and drill exchange</li>
                        <li>Board layout and footprint assignment</li>
                    </ul>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

        <section class="pillars">
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">01</span>
                <h2>Capture</h2>
                <p>
                    Sheets, symbols, nets and references live in the design
                    document, not in a folder of exports. Identities survive every
                    revision.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">02</span>
                <h2>Review</h2>
                <p>
                    Electrical checks report findings with their sheet and object,
                    so a review points at something real instead of a single score.
                    Layout clearance checks are not implemented.
                </p>
            </article>
            <article class="pillar">
                <span class="pillar__index">03</span>
                <h2>Deliver</h2>
                <p>
                    Netlist, SVG, BOM and PDF files are projections of the same
                    revision. KiCad, Gerber and drill output are declared but not
                    implemented.
                </p>
            </article>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Workflow</h2>
                <p>Capture, checks and netlist/SVG/BOM/PDF delivery run today. Board exchange and the interactive canvas do not.</p>
            </div>
            <ol class="steps">
                <li>
                    <span class="steps__index">1</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Declare sheets</h3>
                        <p>Every new design starts with one named sheet and a stable identity.</p>
                        <span class="chip chip--ok">working</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="steps__index">2</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Capture objects</h3>
                        <p>Place components, connect nets and add wires as native objects rather than drawing pixels.</p>
                        <span class="chip chip--ok">working</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="steps__index">3</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Run checks</h3>
                        <p>ERC, net and footprint checks report findings with their sheet and object. DRC, clearance and power do not run.</p>
                        <span class="chip chip--ok">basic</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
                <li>
                    <span class="steps__index">4</span>
                    <div>
                        <h3>Project the revision</h3>
                        <p>Write a netlist, SVG, BOM or one-page PDF from the revision the review saw. KiCad, Gerber and drill are not implemented.</p>
                        <span class="chip chip--ok">net · svg · bom · pdf</span>
                    </div>
                </li>
            </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <div class="section-head">
                <h2>Format matrix</h2>
                <p>Every declared format, with the status the capability matrix reports today.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="table-wrap">
                <table class="table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Format</th>
                            <th>Import</th>
                            <th>Edit</th>
                            <th>Export</th>
                            <th>Status</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr v-for="format in formats" :key="format.name">
                            <td class="cell-mono">{{ format.name }}</td>
                            <td>{{ format.importLevel }}</td>
                            <td>{{ format.editLevel }}</td>
                            <td>{{ format.exportLevel }}</td>
                            <td><span :class="format.tone">{{ format.status }}</span></td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p class="table-note">A suffix is not a support claim. Netlist, SVG, BOM and PDF are export-only projections; no exchange format can be imported or edited.</p>
        </section>

        <section class="status-band">
            <p>
                <b>In development.</b>
                The native model edits one schematic document with bounded undo/redo,
                saves and reopens it, runs ERC, net and footprint checks, and writes
                netlist, SVG, BOM or PDF. The interactive renderer, KiCad/Gerber
                exchange, drill and board layout report
                <code>capability/not-implemented</code>.
            </p>
            <Link to="RoadmapPage" class="btn btn--ghost">
                See the order of work
            </Link>
        </section>

        <section class="cta-band">
            <div>
                <span class="eyebrow">Source first</span>
                <h2>Read the contracts before the claims.</h2>
                <p>
